<title>USA: Cleveland schools reach teacher pact.</title>
<headline>Cleveland schools reach teacher pact.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cleveland City School District reached a tentative agreement with its 5,000-member teachers union early Sunday averting a strike that had been due to start at midnight, local media reported.</p>
<p>WEWS-TV reported that a three-year tentative pact was reached including a two-year wage freeze and a raise during the third year. The former contract expired Sept. 3, but was extended to enable contract negotiations to continue.</p>
<p>The Cleveland schools are controlled by the state of Ohio.</p>
</text>
